/T (LOC8 does not use a database server. In line with the File Handling objective of the course, all information is kept in ordinary files inside a data folder that the application creates on first run. This keeps the application self-contained and easy to copy or back up, and it removes any installation or configuration step for the user.)
/E (LOC8 does not use a database server. In line with the File Handling objective of the course, all information is kept in ordinary files inside a data folder that the application creates on first run. This keeps the application self-contained and easy to copy or back up, and it removes any installation or configuration step for the user.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
