343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 157 0 R
/T (Three kinds of files are used, each chosen for the kind of data it holds. Lost and found reports are Java objects with several fields and a variable number of records, so they are saved by object serialisation. Campus locations and emergency contacts are simple rows of text that the campus staff may want to edit by hand, so they are kept in CSV files. Pictures attached to reports are copied into an images folder and referred to by their path.)
/E (Three kinds of files are used, each chosen for the kind of data it holds. Lost and found reports are Java objects with several fields and a variable number of records, so they are saved by object serialisation. Campus locations and emergency contacts are simple rows of text that the campus staff may want to edit by hand, so they are kept in CSV files. Pictures attached to reports are copied into an images folder and referred to by their path.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
