377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 159 0 R
/T (LOC8 follows a layered design that separates what the user sees from the rules of the application and from the way data are stored. The Presentation Layer consists of the Swing window and its panels. The Logic Layer consists of the model classes and the SearchService. The Data Layer consists of the DataStore class, which is the only class that reads or writes files. Because of this separation, the storage method could be replaced later \(for example by a database\) by changing DataStore alone.)
/E (LOC8 follows a layered design that separates what the user sees from the rules of the application and from the way data are stored. The Presentation Layer consists of the Swing window and its panels. The Logic Layer consists of the model classes and the SearchService. The Data Layer consists of the DataStore class, which is the only class that reads or writes files. Because of this separation, the storage method could be replaced later \(for example by a database\) by changing DataStore alone.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
