2022 0 obj
<<
/Title (LOC8 does not use a database server. In line with the File Handling objective of the course, all information is kept in ordinary files inside a data folder that the application creates on first run. This keeps the application self-contained and easy to copy or back up, and it removes any installation or configuration step for the user.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2018 0 R
/Next 2023 0 R
>>
endobj
2023 0 obj
<<
/Title (Three kinds of files are used, each chosen for the kind of data it holds. Lost and found reports are Java objects with several fields and a variable number of records, so they are saved by object serialisation. Campus locations and emergency contacts are simple rows of text that the campus staff may want to edit by hand, so they are kept in CSV files. Pictures attached to reports are copied into an images folder and referred to by their path.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2018 0 R
/Prev 2022 0 R
>>
endobj
2024 0 obj
<<
/Title (4.2 FILE STRUCTURE AND RECORD FORMATS)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2016 0 R
/Prev 2018 0 R
/First 2029 0 R
/Last 2029 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 2019 0 R
>>
endobj
2025 0 obj
<<
/Title (Several safeguards protect the stored data. The report form refuses to save a report unless the item name, place and contact are filled in. When saving, the program first writes the complete list to a temporary file and only then replaces items.dat, so an interruption during the write cannot leave a half-written file. When loading, a missing items file gives an empty list, a damaged items file is ignored instead of crashing the program, and CSV rows that do not have the expected number of fields are skipped. These behaviours were checked with a small test program that exercises the real DataStore and SearchService classes \(Chapter 6, Table 6.1\). The tests confirm that saved reports reload with their fields intact, that the recovered status persists, that images are copied with their extension kept, that a malformed CSV row is skipped and that a corrupt items file is handled without an error.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2020 0 R
/First 2030 0 R
/Last 2030 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 2026 0 R
>>
endobj
