2050 0 obj
<<
/Title (The main window \(LOC8App\) is a JFrame containing a JTabbedPane with three tabs. The Lost & Found tab \(LostFoundPanel\) has a form on the left for reporting an item, a JTable in the centre listing all reports with a search box above it, and buttons to mark a report as recovered or to delete it. Selecting a row with a picture displays a scaled preview. A JFileChooser restricted to JPG and PNG files is used to attach an image. The Campus Search and Emergency Contacts tabs reuse one generic panel, EntityListPanel<T>. It contains a search box, a result list and a detail area. A DocumentListener refilters the list after every keystroke, so results update as the user types. The only difference between the two tabs is the data supplied and a small function that formats the detail text, which is an example of how inheritance and generics reduce duplicated code.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2044 0 R
/First 2055 0 R
/Last 2055 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 2051 0 R
>>
endobj
